  "final_answer": "The 404 came from a wrong URL in the client. The tests pass, but I haven't run the app against a live backend.\n\n**Cause:** `suggestions.ts` posted to `/api/recommend`, and the backend has no route at that path. The only recommendation route is `POST /api/colleges/recommend`, in `python-backend/api/routes.py`. The other client callers (`collegeApi.ts` and `useCollegeListGenerator.ts`) already use the correct path.\n\n**Second problem:** The old request body would have failed even with the right URL. `suggestions.ts` sent `{student_id, answers}`, but the backend's `RecommendRequest` requires `{student_profile: {answers: ...}}`. It would have returned a 422 error instead. This is the same shape the working generator hook sends.\n\n**Fix:** I changed both calls in `suggestions.ts`, `generateSuggestedColleges` and `generateSuggestedCollegesFromAnswers`:\n- The URL is now `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n- The body is now `{ student_profile: { answers } }`.\n\nI did not add a second `/api/recommend` route to the backend, so there is still exactly one recommendation endpoint.\n\n**Files changed:** only `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`.",
